I don't know that the following is relevant, but just in case:

I had similar-sounding problems with recovering an apparently
corrupted savegame a few weeks ago, albeit on Windows. Nethack had
apparently crashed upon startup (I was recklessly trying to run it in
funky terminal types instead of standard DOS boxes) and left my
savegame not in its normal 'single file' state, but split up into one
file per dungeon level, as it does while you are playing. Nethack
refused to start, telling me the game was apparently still in
progress, instead of offering me the 'recover?' prompt that I
expected.

After a few days messing with it, I belatedly realised that the old
nethack process, the original one which I thought had crashed, was
actually still running in the background - so the game *was* still in
progress, albeit invisibly. The computer had been turned off each
night, but of course I was only hibernating, not actually shutting
down. Killing this process manually allowed the next invocation of
nethack to kick into 'recover' mode.

I dunno if there is some equivalent scenario on the mac, but it seems
possible.



